  "id": "spindle-waves",
  "term": "spindle waves",
  "definition": "Spindle waves are spindle-like patterns of brain electrical activity seen on the EEG during general anesthesia, also described as anesthesia alpha oscillations. They appear with several anesthetic drugs and have been proposed as possible signs of anesthesia depth and level of unconsciousness.",
